<article class="env-lemma" id="03S1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03S1">Lemma <span data-tag="03S1">59.72.2</span>.</a> Let $f: X \to Y$ be a morphism of schemes which is quasi-compact, quasi-separated, and locally of finite type. If $\eta $ is a generic point of an irreducible component of $Y$ such that $f^{-1}(\eta )$ is finite, then there exists an open $V \subset Y$ containing $\eta $ such that $f^{-1}(V) \to V$ is finite. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02NW" data-tag="02NW">29.52.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>